# R41 T-FMT-A — the NAMED-argument ownership position, `&` cell.
#
# AXIS CELL: `CallArg.ownership` on a NAMED argument. `parse_call_arg` runs
# `parse_ownership_modifier` BEFORE the `name =` lookahead, so the sigil slot is
# ahead of the NAME (`&b = x`, the D35 spelling) — not after the `=`.
#
# INTENDED: runs and prints `2`, before AND after `gg fmt`. Pre-fix the
# formatter emitted the name first and the sigil after the `=`
# (`takes_mut(1, b = &x)`), putting it where the pre-pass cannot see it: the
# sigil was re-parsed as part of the VALUE and `CallArg.ownership` came back
# `Borrow`. A WORKING program became 2 semantic errors
# (E_OwnershipMismatch + E_AmpInOperandPosition).
#
# The seed is COMPUTED so no const-fold can elide the call.

void takes_mut(int a, int &b):
    b = b + 1

int seed():
    return 1

void main():
    int x = seed()
    takes_mut(1, &b = x)
    print(x)
